  "details": "Quest players has been having the issue of “You have been sent home your system ran out of memory” error for months now. Before late July going into August it would randomly happen but would eventually still allow Quest players to get into worlds without being sent back home or completely crashing. But sometime during late July going into to August after a few updates this issue has skyrocketed and become much worse. (In the screenshot of a previous report) This is essentially what continues to happen. In more detail I load up VRChat on Quest and in my old home I would get stuck in a cycle of blue screen (being hit with the loading screen) because it was trying to send me back to home when I never loaded into it in the first place. My old home world was 90mb and I’ve never had a problem loading into it until late July. I had another homeworld that was 97mb and it has done the same as the previous one. My cache has been cleared frequently not even nearing the 4gb limit and it still occurs. It’s not a Quest system memory because I’m only using 104 out of 128gb. I have tried deleting and reinstalling, that didn’t help. Even loading in worlds with low megabyte count has crashed me. \n\nPlease look into and fix this issue. It has been extremely frustrating and demotivating for me to play VRChat as much as I use to. \n\nI as well as many Quest can even load into great worlds we’ve already been to without being sent back to home or crashing as of this current build. PS I had a video of it happening but the file limit prevented me from sending it.",
